--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/neoism-device-preview.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+---
+"@gpuix/native": patch
+---
+
+Add an off-by-default `device-preview` binding with four distinct original indexed-mesh profiles: iphone-18-pro, iphone-18-pro-max, iphone-duo and ipad-pro-13-m5, plus an original tablet keyboard/stand accessory. Use same-device GPUI wgpu texture composition, a depth buffer, 4× MSAA, finish-aware studio reflections, bounded latest-frame RGBA uploads, and no browser or production readback. Existing GPUI `gpu_context` and `paint_surface` APIs suffice; upstream symbol search found no additional API needed (https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues?q=gpu_context+paint_surface).
+
+Replace fullscreen raymarching with reusable vertex/index buffers, native mesh-authoritative picking and visible-display selection. Include detailed bevels/glass, ports, speaker perforations, buttons/seams, camera platforms and lens assemblies, articulated inner/cover Duo screens and keyboard/trackpad geometry. Preserve live whites and contain-fit screen UVs; pose changes do not reupload video. Headless screenshot tests cover the original lineup front/back and accessories under artifacts/device-preview; readback exists only in tests. Linux is validated; FreeBSD remains unvalidated. No copied meshes, GLBs or textures are included, and proportions are original designs rather than official CAD.
+
+Correct the tablet accessory to landscape with a wide base, support/hinge, keys and trackpad; remap screen UVs so landscape video stays upright and native picking follows the same transformed mesh. Add landscape color-card screenshot evidence and an accessories contact sheet. Allow exactly PI fold for a truly closed Duo with a minimal 0.02-unit inner-glass clearance, and improve studio gradients and glass/lens clearcoat without extra passes.
+
+Substantively reauthor the original profiles against local visual references: wide Pro camera shelves and inset glass, correct triangular lens placement, convex optical caps/coatings, thin rounded rails, near-identical normalized Pro/Max screen aspects, a black tablet/keyboard with geometric legends, and a portrait top/bottom Duo with vertical dual-camera pill and lower outside cover. Replace exponent highlights/Reinhard with linear GGX/Smith/Schlick, exact sRGB transfer, reference lighting and analytic softbox room reflections. Use native bounds framing at 32 degrees (36 for Duo), dead-front default pose, and exact unlit video bytes. Add matched-camera/frame before-after PNGs and separately fitted neutral-wallpaper proofs; no copied model/texture payloads or brand logos.
+
+Accept confirmed host orientation for bare phones/tablets, rotate all physical geometry and remap landscape video upright with matching native picks. Do not double-rotate keyboard or Duo. Fix optional renderer automation bounds queries to read the published painted map instead of blocking on the UI queue. Wire explicit Linux captureScreenshot commands to the independently pinned GPUI same-window scene capture API on the UI thread, saving PNG and responding immediately without waiting for a future frame. This adds no viewport or idle readback; headless fixture tests do not stand in for a production full-panel capture, which must be exercised on the running optimized app.
+
+Add default-off duoBook presentation for the original Duo rig. Preserve portrait-clamshell fixtures while allowing the broad, slightly folded side-by-side book hold. Rotate raw portrait inner frames into book UVs exactly once and accept already-landscape frames without double rotation; the native closest-triangle pick returns matching raw frame coordinates. Include book/raw-versus-prepared GPU equivalence, closed-cover facing/picking, mesh-cache-key tests, and live/offline book PNG proofs. Preserve the parent preview artwork, 1536 render cap, transparent full-window anchored portals and explicit window capture.
